    "## Robustness Calculation\n",
    "\n",
    "According to the IEEE CAI 2026 paper, robustness is defined as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$r(C, x) = 1 - \\frac{\\max_{\\text{ICF} \\in AR_{C,y}} \\text{cost}_x(\\text{ICF})}{|\\text{features}|}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "- $C$ is the classifier\n",
    "- $x$ is the sample\n",
    "- $y = C(x)$ is the classification\n",
    "- $AR_{C,y}$ is the set of Anti-Reasons for class $y$\n",
    "- $\\text{cost}_x(\\text{ICF})$ is the cost function for ICF applied to sample $x$\n",
    "- $|\\text{features}|$ is the total number of features\n",
    "\n",
    "The robustness measure quantifies how resistant a sample is to classification changes:\n",
    "- A value of 0 indicates no robustness (classifier decision changes easily)\n",
    "- A value of 1 denotes maximum robustness (sample is completely stable)"
